// t_61109061 PROTOTYPE CELL.  The semantic that is JUDGED is the one on the
// FIRST DECLARATION in source order; the body that is WALKED is the
// DEFINITION's.  Measured on sce-cgc 475 - the four cells disagree, so neither
// "judge the definition" nor "judge either" reproduces the reference.
//
// prototype BARE, definition :COLOR - the cell that forbids judging the\n// DEFINITION: the reference ACCEPTS this.
// Compile with -e beta.  Reference verdict: ACCEPT
float4 gamma(float4 t);
float4 gamma(float4 t) : COLOR { return t*2.0; }
float4 beta(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return gamma(t)*0.5; }
